The image is labeled "LT LAT", indicating a left lateral chest X-ray. In a standard left lateral view, the patient's left side is against the detector (or closest to it depending on convention, but usually "Left Lateral" means left side down). However, determining atelectasis location (right vs left base) from a single lateral view without a frontal reference can be challenging due to superimposition.

Let's use `chest_xray_expert` to get a focused interpretation of this specific lateral view regarding basal opacities.

